## Why This Is Asked

Real-time, asynchronous, event-driven integrations with external partners are inherently error-prone. This question evaluates understanding of contract testing, schema evolution strategy, latency SLAs, idempotency, and resilience patterns—all critical for payment infrastructure reliability.

## Key Concepts

- Consumer-driven contracts (Pact) for multi-party API agreements
- Backward-compatible schema evolution with feature-flagged payloads
- Async webhook reliability: retries, dead-letter queues, circuit breakers
- End-to-end latency measurement with OpenTelemetry distributed tracing

## Code Example

